# ignore folder
zephyrproject
tools/*
build*
models/

# a retired generated directory from before the trees under src/deps were
# committed: src/external/ came from `deploy_akida_engine`. Kept ignored so a
# stale working copy stays harmless.
src/external/

# the Akida engine's own test tree. `akida engine deploy` has no flag to skip
# it, no build ever compiles it, and test/akd1000/test_fnp2/program.cpp alone is
# 9.3 MB of fixtures for the AKD1000, which this firmware does not target. The
# rest of src/deps is tracked deliberately.
src/deps/akida/engine/test/

# ignore specific files
*JLink_Linux_V888_x86_64.deb

# safety
.env/*
*.pem
*.key

# but allow
!.env/README.md

# The development signing key is committed on purpose and must survive both
# rules above. It is not a secret; the file's own header explains why. Its
# sibling .env/production_key.pem is the real secret, is written only by
# .github/workflows/release.yml during a release build, and has no exception
# here or anywhere else: it stays ignored by .env/* and by *.pem.
!.env/development_key.pem

# misc files
*.DS_Store

# all local
*local*

# local-only working files
.plans/
.userguide/
.helpers/
*__pycache__*
scripts/sync.sh